# CodeMie — Brand Compliance API
# (+ optional Figma import for CHMarketingBuilder)

Server-side environment variables for the Vercel embed API used by `CHBrandCompliance`.

See also: [api/lib/codemie/README.md](./lib/codemie/README.md) for full auth flow, troubleshooting, and the smoke-test script.

---

## Required (embed API)

```env
# Shared secret — same value as apiToken in Content Hub component config
BRAND_COMPLIANCE_API_SECRET=your-secure-token

# CodeMie assistant UUID from CodeMie UI (copy from your assistant page)
CODEMIE_BRAND_COMPLIANCE_ASSISTANT_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx

# Fine Art Tagging Analyst assistant (CHFineArtTagging)
CODEMIE_FINE_ART_TAGGING_ASSISTANT_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional dedicated embed secret for fine-art tagging (falls back to BRAND_COMPLIANCE_API_SECRET)
# FINE_ART_TAGGING_API_SECRET=your-secure-token
```

`CODEMIE_MY_AGENT_ASSISTANT_ID` is also accepted as a fallback assistant ID.

---

## CodeMie API (always set for non-static-token auth)

```env
CODEMIE_API_URL=https://codemie.lab.epam.com/code-assistant-api
```

---

## CodeMie authentication — pick one block

Auth is auto-detected. You do **not** need `CODEMIE_USE_KEYCLOAK_AUTH=true` when username + password are set.

### A) Client secret — recommended for production / CI / shared servers

```env
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=your-service-account-client-id
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_REALM=codemie-prod
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_SERVER_URL=https://auth.codemie.lab.epam.com
```

No username or password. Uses `grant_type=client_credentials`.

### B) User password grant — dev, personal scripts, quick integration testing

Same path Signal-Monitor uses. **Not ideal for production** (password in env is a security risk).

```env
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=codemie-sdk
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_USERNAME=you@epam.com
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_PASSWORD=your-password
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_REALM=codemie-prod
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_SERVER_URL=https://auth.codemie.lab.epam.com
```

| Variable | Example | Purpose |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID` | `codemie-sdk` | Keycloak OAuth client. `codemie-sdk` is the standard public client for user login. |
| `CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_USERNAME` | your EPAM email | Your CodeMie/EPAM account username |
| `CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_PASSWORD` | your password | Your account password |
| `CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_REALM` | `codemie-prod` | Keycloak realm CodeMie uses in EPAM lab |
| `CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_SERVER_URL` | `https://auth.codemie.lab.epam.com` | Where to request tokens |

At runtime the server exchanges these for a JWT:

```http
POST https://auth.codemie.lab.epam.com/realms/codemie-prod/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=codemie-sdk&username=you@epam.com&password=your-password
```

The `access_token` is cached for ~55 minutes, then refreshed automatically.

### C) Static bearer token — quick test only (expires, manual refresh)

```env
CODEMIE_API_KEY=eyJ...
```

---

## Complete .env example — Option B (dev)

```env
# Embed API
BRAND_COMPLIANCE_API_SECRET=your-secure-token
BRAND_COMPLIANCE_CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-content-hub-origin.sitecoresandbox.cloud

# Auth — user password grant
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=codemie-sdk
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_USERNAME=you@epam.com
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_PASSWORD=your-password
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_REALM=codemie-prod
CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_SERVER_URL=https://auth.codemie.lab.epam.com

# API
CODEMIE_API_URL=https://codemie.lab.epam.com/code-assistant-api

# Your agents
CODEMIE_BRAND_COMPLIANCE_ASSISTANT_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
CODEMIE_FINE_ART_TAGGING_ASSISTANT_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
```

---

## Optional

```env
BRAND_COMPLIANCE_CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-content-hub-origin.sitecoresandbox.cloud
AI_DEBUG=true
```

`BRAND_COMPLIANCE_CORS_ORIGIN` accepts comma-separated origins. When omitted, CORS allows `*`.

---

## Figma import (CHMarketingBuilder)

Used by `POST /api/figma/import` to turn a Figma frame into template zones.

```env
# Required — Figma personal access token (file must be accessible to this token)
FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN=figd_xxxxxxxx

# Optional — Bearer secret for the import endpoint.
# Falls back to BRAND_COMPLIANCE_API_SECRET when set.
# Pass the same value as figmaImportApiToken in the Marketing Builder component config.
FIGMA_IMPORT_API_SECRET=your-secure-token
```

Designer naming on Figma layers:

```
zone:headline | type:Heading | label:Headline
zone:hero | type:Image
zone:body | type:Text
zone:logo | type:Logo
zone:cta | type:CTA Button
```

Copy the frame link from Figma (must include `node-id`) and use **Import from Figma** in Template admin.

---

## Quick test — Keycloak auth (Option B)

```bash
curl -X POST "https://auth.codemie.lab.epam.com/realms/codemie-prod/protocol/openid-connect/token" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded" \
  -d "grant_type=password&client_id=codemie-sdk&username=YOU@epam.com&password=YOUR_PASSWORD"
```

If that returns `access_token`, auth is working.

## Quick test — assistant call

```bash
curl -X POST "https://codemie.lab.epam.com/code-assistant-api/v1/assistants/YOUR_ASSISTANT_ID/model" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -d '{"text":"Hello from Brand Compliance","stream":false}'
```

Expected response shape:

```json
{
  "generated": "...assistant reply...",
  "timeElapsed": 1.2,
  "tokensUsed": null
}
```

## Quick test — embed API (full stack)

```bash
curl -X POST "https://YOUR-PROJECT.vercel.app/api/brand-compliance/analyze" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_BRAND_COMPLIANCE_API_SECRET" \
  -d '{"asset":{"id":"123","name":"Hero banner","fileName":"hero-banner.jpg","mimeType":"image/jpeg","description":"Homepage hero"}}'
```

## Node smoke test (uses env vars directly)

```bash
# PowerShell — set vars then run
$env:CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID="codemie-sdk"
$env:CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_USERNAME="you@epam.com"
$env:CODEMIE_KEYCLOAK_PASSWORD="your-password"
$env:CODEMIE_BRAND_COMPLIANCE_ASSISTANT_ID="your-assistant-uuid"
npm run codemie:smoke
```

---

## Common issues

| Symptom | Likely cause |
|---------|----------------|
| 401 from Keycloak | Wrong username/password, or account not in `codemie-prod` realm |
| HTML instead of JSON from CodeMie API | Token invalid or expired |
| 403 on assistant call | Assistant not shared with your account |
| Works locally, fails in CI | Password grant blocked or unsuitable for CI — use client secret (Option A) |
